   "text": "dev is protected: never push dev; branch and open a PR into dev (memory dev-branch-protected, 2026-10-23)"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "research",
   "text": "oh one other thing we need to take into consideration...we need a control panel for the processing engine.  a way to control the flow of the data through the engine (Kafka)."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "so in short, what we need are 1. control panel to monitor and manage the processor 2. the lab in 48 3. all settings other than database connection information stored in the database like we always do. 4. real-time reporting on progress and status 5. exportable html reports on progress to users"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "and 6.  and this is the main one, we need a chat process that can do all of the above through chat as well as have a conversation with the user about optimization of processing."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "and 7.  We need to be able to connect to the fusion-sql-mcp server"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "that's where we will connect to fusion to search for receipts and invoices"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "I like the idea of the fusion traffic being direct but the mcp server also provides value because  there's no thinking about connectivity...it just works.  so we're going to go through the MCP server for fusion connectivity"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-23",
   "step": "design",
   "text": "sorry...I meant to say the mcp server will be used to read from fusion, write to fusion via REST however, the receipt SOAP call will be done from the API"
  }
 ],
